{
 "id": "araxxor",
 "name": "Araxxor",
 "wikiUrl": "https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Araxxor",
 "overview": [
  "As with all araxytes, Araxxor’s attacks can inflict venom. He spawns in the centre of his chamber and primarily attacks with melee. If the player is outside melee range, Araxxor will close the distance and attack with either magic or ranged, selecting whichever targets the player’s lower Defence roll [2]. Aranea boots can be worn to negate damage from his ranged attack once every 8 ticks (every other attack); however, they do not protect against his magic attacks.",
  "Around Araxxor’s lair are nine eggs—three red, three white, and three green. The first egg hatches after three standard attacks from Araxxor, beginning clockwise from the south-easternmost egg. Each subsequent egg hatches after every six standard attacks. Both the eggs and the araxytes spawned from them count as on-task monsters for the purpose of receiving the slayer helmet damage bonus, but the spawned araxytes do not reduce the player’s task kill count.",
  "Every six standard attacks, Araxxor will use one of three special attacks. The special attack can be identified by the colour of the south-easternmost egg:",
  "* Red egg first – Acid Drip: Acid lands beneath the player and follows their movement for several seconds. * White egg first – Acid Spray: Acid sprays randomly outward in the player’s general direction. * Green egg first – Acid Bullet: An acid projectile travels in a straight line toward the player, leaving a trail of acid and creating an acid spray when it impacts the cave wall. * All of these attacks leave acid pools, which inflict venom and deal increasingly larger damage (starting from 4) the longer the player stays on them.",
  "When Araxxor reaches 25% health, he enters an enrage phase. During this phase, his Defence level increases by 35 and his attack speed increases from 6 ticks to 4 ticks. He also replaces his melee attack with a cleave attack for the remainder of the fight. The cleave deals melee damage in a 1×3 area and leaves acid pools on the ground. If the player steps underneath Araxxor during the attack, the cleave can damage him and the affected area is reduced to 1×1. As with his ranged attack, aranea boots can negate damage from the cleave once every 12 seconds (20 ticks).",
  "Finally, be cautious around the edges of the room, as some tiles may appear walkable but cannot be moved onto."
 ],
